     1	# fable5-skills
     2	
     3	11 Agent Skills written for how Claude Fable 5 and Mythos-class deployments
     4	actually behave, independently designed for this series after auditing (not
     5	reusing) a third-party collection. See Part 6 of the Substack series for the
     6	audit and the design notes.
     7	
     8	| # | Skill | What it fixes |
     9	|---|-------|---------------|
    10	| 1 | [`effort-router`](effort-router/SKILL.md) | Picking and re-evaluating `output_config.effort` per workload instead of carrying over an old model's defaults. |
    11	| 2 | [`scope-fence`](scope-fence/SKILL.md) | Unrequested actions -- applying a fix when only asked to diagnose, restarting a service, backup branches nobody asked for. |
    12	| 3 | [`no-gold-plating`](no-gold-plating/SKILL.md) | Diffs bigger than the ask: speculative abstractions, defensive checks for impossible states. |
    13	| 4 | [`evidence-bound-progress`](evidence-bound-progress/SKILL.md) | Status reports on long runs bound to an actual tool result, never a fabricated "tests passing". |
    14	| 5 | [`act-on-sufficiency`](act-on-sufficiency/SKILL.md) | Over-planning and re-deriving settled facts at high effort. |
    15	| 6 | [`verifier-subagent`](verifier-subagent/SKILL.md) | Fresh-context verifier subagents instead of self-critique; the maker never grades its own work. |
    16	| 7 | [`autonomy-contract`](autonomy-contract/SKILL.md) | Unattended runs that stall on a stated intent or a mid-run permission question. |
    17	| 8 | [`lesson-memory`](lesson-memory/SKILL.md) | File-based cross-session memory, with the anti-poisoning gate a shared lesson file needs. |
    18	| 9 | [`reader-first-summary`](reader-first-summary/SKILL.md) | Final reports readable by someone who saw none of the work -- no arrow chains, no invented shorthand. |
    19	| 10 | [`refusal-aware-calling`](refusal-aware-calling/SKILL.md) | `claude-fable-5` calls that degrade gracefully on a classifier refusal instead of dead-ending. |
    20	| 11 | [`mythos-scope-gate`](mythos-scope-gate/SKILL.md) | Approved Mythos-style cyber work must carry authorization, bounded targets, private artifacts, independent validation, and a patch owner. |
    21	
    22	## Install
    23	
    24	**Claude Code, as a plugin:**
    25	
    26	```
    27	/plugin marketplace add kenhuangus/fable5
    28	/plugin install fable5-skills@fable5
    29	```
    30	
    31	**Manual, per skill:**
    32	
    33	```bash
    34	git clone https://github.com/kenhuangus/fable5
    35	cp -r fable5/skills/scope-fence ~/.claude/skills/
    36	```
    37	
    38	## How they activate
    39	
    40	`effort-router`, `verifier-subagent`, and `lesson-memory` are task-shaped and
    41	trigger automatically when a matching request appears. The rest are standing
    42	behavioral rules -- a model mid-over-planning won't reliably invoke
    43	`act-on-sufficiency` on its own. For those, either invoke explicitly in an
    44	interactive session, or copy the skill body into your system prompt /
    45	`CLAUDE.md` for unattended pipelines (`autonomy-contract` is written for
    46	exactly that case).

